{"name":"Tretinoin for beard","deep":true,"image":null,"mentions":26,"casual":{"lead":["Tretinoin is a prescription vitamin A derivative used on skin for acne and photoaging. In beard-growth forums it is layered with minoxidil in hopes of getting denser facial hair than minoxidil alone.","The proposed link is that tretinoin increases how much minoxidil converts to its active sulfate form. A general reference describes tretinoin combined with minoxidil in hair-loss studies, with evidence it calls weak and contradictory. No beard studies were found."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["It is applied topically with a minoxidil product as an off-label combination, in a skincare-style routine. Results from minoxidil on the beard are generally described as building over months."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["Topical use commonly causes redness, peeling, irritation and sun sensitivity. Oral tretinoin is contraindicated in pregnancy. It is prescription-only in the US, UK and EU."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[],"links":{"studies":[{"title":"Drugs for acne.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38294764/","source":"The Medical letter on drugs and therapeutics","year":2024,"cites":null,"kind":null},{"title":"Drugs for acne.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33443492/","source":"The Medical letter on drugs and therapeutics","year":2020,"cites":null,"kind":null},{"title":"Schools of pharmacology: retinoid update.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17039662/","source":"Journal of drugs in dermatology : JDD","year":2006,"cites":null,"kind":"Review"},{"title":"Safety and efficacy of Tretin-X compared with Retin-A in patients with mild-to-severe acne vulgaris.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16687979/","source":"Skinmed","year":2006,"cites":null,"kind":"Randomized Controlled Trial"},{"title":"Role of mild cleansing in the management of patient skin.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/14728696/","source":"Dermatologic therapy","ye