-skin.54782/"},{"title":"should i be exfoliating while on retin a","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/should-i-be-exfoliating-while-on-retin-a.53414/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220817095508/https://looksmax.org/threads/should-i-be-exfoliating-while-on-retin-a.53414/"},{"title":"dont use retin a as a young person","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/dont-use-retin-a-as-a-young-person.53068/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220811001614/https://looksmax.org/threads/dont-use-retin-a-as-a-young-person.53068/"},{"title":"how to use retin a 0 05 liquid","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/how-to-use-retin-a-0-05-liquid.52943/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230328190052/https://looksmax.org/threads/how-to-use-retin-a-0-05-liquid.52943/"},{"title":"whats the ideal retin a to use","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/whats-the-ideal-retin-a-to-use.11851/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250715093930/https://looksmax.org/threads/whats-the-ideal-retin-a-to-use.11851/"},{"title":"the looksmaxxers guide to retin a tretinoin skinmaxxers acnecels gtfih","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/the-looksmaxxers-guide-to-retin-a-tretinoin-skinmaxxers-acnecels-gtfih.6107/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20210831045447/https://looksmax.org/threads/the-looksmaxxers-guide-to-retin-a-tretinoin-skinmaxxers-acnecels-gtfih.6107/"},{"title":"gunna buy retin a","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/gunna-buy-retin-a.3495/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230528140551/https://looksmax.org/threads/gunna-buy-retin-a.3495/"}],"news":[],"social":[],"web":[{"title":"Tretinoin (Wikipedia)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tretinoin"},{"title":"Minoxidil (Wikipedia)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minoxidil"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Hair (facial/body)","chain":["Tretinoin thins skin barrier","Minoxidil absorbs more readily","More beard growth at follicles"],"effect":"claimed","text":"The idea is that tretinoin helps minoxidil absorb and convert more readily, so beard follicles get a stronger growth push. It is discussed online as an off-label combination; beard-specific evidence for the tretinoin addition is lacking."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":null,"lead":["Tretinoin (all-trans retinoic acid) is a retinoid prescribed mainly for acne, and for photoaging; the oral form treats acute promyelocytic leukemia.[1] In some beard-growth routines it is combined with minoxidil, which is approved for scalp hair loss and used off-label for beard growth.[2]","Wikipedia reports tretinoin has been studied with minoxidil for hair loss, partly for its possible ability to increase minoxidil sulfate production, and describes the evidence as weak and contradictory.[1] No studies found on tretinoin for beard growth."],"infobox":[["Drug class","Retinoid (vitamin A derivative)"],["Routes","Topical (oral for leukemia)[1]"],["Approved for acne (US)","1971[1]"],["Brand names","Retin-A, Avita, Renova[1]"],["Legal status","Rx-only (US, UK, EU)[1]"]],"sections":[{"h":"Pharmacology","paras":["In skin, tretinoin binds retinoic acid receptors and retinoid X receptors in keratinocytes, normalizing follicle keratinization and reducing inflammation signaling.[1] Minoxidil is a prodrug converted by sulfotransferase enzymes to minoxidil sulfate, which is the active form.[2]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Adverse effects","paras":["Topical use can cause irritation, redness, peeling, blistering and increased sun sensitivity.[1] Oral tretinoin is contraindicated in pregnancy because of birth-defect risk; Australia rates the topical form category D.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"History","paras":["Tretinoin was patented in 1957 and approved for medical use in 1962; it was developed for acne at the University of Pennsylvania by James Fulton and Albert Kligman and FDA-approved for acne in 1971.[1] Minoxidil was named in 1963, introduced for hypertension in 1971, and approved topically for male baldness in 1988.[2]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found for beard growth. A general reference describes studies of tretinoin plus minoxidil for scalp hair loss with weak and contradictory evidence.[1]"],"subs":[]}],"lore":{"intro":"Tretinoin appears in beard forums as an add-on to minoxidil.","claims":[{"claim":"Adding tretinoin to minoxidil increases absorption and beard results.","verdict":"unknown","note":""}]},"timeline":[{"year":"1957","event":"Tretinoin patented.[1]"},{"year":"1971","event":"FDA approves tretinoin for acne.[1]"},{"year":"1988","event":"Topical minoxidil approved for male baldness (Rogaine).[2]"}],"refs":[{"title":"Tretinoin (Wikipedia)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tretinoin","source":"Wikipedia","year":null,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Minoxidil (Wikipedia)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minoxidil","source":"Wikipedia","year":null,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[{"title":"Tretinoin (Wikipedia)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tretinoin","source":"Wikipedia","year":null,"kind":null}],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Discussion Retin-A on eyelids: risk of getting MGD or dry/red eyes?","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/retin-a-on-eyelids-risk-of-getting-mgd-or-dry-red-eyes.572036/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220920180953/https://looksmax.org/threads/retin-a-on-eyelids-risk-of-getting-mgd-or-dry-red-eyes.572036/"},{"title":"LifeFuel Retin A does burn fat on the face","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/retin-a-does-burn-fat-on-the-face.495707/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220513134223/https://looksmax.org/threads/retin-a-does-burn-fat-on-the-face.495707/"},{"title":"retin a since 22 and dutasteride + dermarolling since 25 (28 now)","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/retin-a-since-22-and-dutasteride-dermarolling-since-25-28-now.433290/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20211218203007/https://looksmax.org/threads/retin-a-since-22-and-dutasteride-dermarolling-since-25-28-now.433290/"},{"title":"retin a and hairloss","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/retin-a-and-hairloss.259040/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20221126214145/https://looksmax.org/threads/retin-a-and-hairloss.259040/"},{"title":"retin a or diuretics to burn face fat","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/retin-a-or-diuretics-to-burn-face-fat.176369/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260427132104/https://looksmax.org/threads/retin-a-or-diuretics-to-burn-face-fat.176369/"},{"title":"retin a causes loss of subcutaneous fat","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/retin-a-causes-loss-of-subcutaneous-fat.135795/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20211107201117/https://looksmax.org/threads/retin-a-causes-loss-of-subcutaneous-fat.135795/"},{"title":"how long does your retin a tube last","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/how-long-does-your-retin-a-tube-last.572017/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220920180953/https://looksmax.org/threads/how-long-does-your-retin-a-tube-last.572017/"},{"title":"does applying retin a 0 05 twice give the same results as 0 1 once","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/does-applying-retin-a-0-05-twice-give-the-same-results-as-0-1-once.559680/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220901233241/https://looksmax.org/threads/does-applying-retin-a-0-05-twice-give-the-same-results-as-0-1-once.559680/"},{"title":"does applying moisturizer after treatment retin a rub off the treatment","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/does-applying-moisturizer-after-treatment-retin-a-rub-off-the-treatment.557182/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220830133137/https://looksmax.org/threads/does-applying-moisturizer-after-treatment-retin-a-rub-off-the-treatment.557182/"},{"title":"does retin a shrink nose","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/does-retin-a-shrink-nose.519097/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220720041941/https://looksmax.org/threads/does-retin-a-shrink-nose.519097/"},{"title":"how effective will tretinoin retin a be for reducing buccal fat","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/how-effective-will-tretinoin-retin-a-be-for-reducing-buccal-fat.493474/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220430222920/https://looksmax.org/threads/how-effective-will-tretinoin-retin-a-be-for-reducing-buccal-fat.493474/"},{"title":"warning for tretinoin retin a users meibomian glands","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/warning-for-tretinoin-retin-a-users-meibomian-glands.482402/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220803224839/https://looksmax.org/threads/warning-for-tretinoin-retin-a-users-meibomian-glands.482402/"},{"title":"rashes from retin a use","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/rashes-from-retin-a-use.466337/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220309051737/https://looksmax.org/threads/rashes-from-retin-a-use.466337/"},{"title":"extremely red face not acne while using retin a","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/extremely-red-face-not-acne-while-using-retin-a.360684/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20210611231911/https://looksmax.org/threads/extremely-red-face-not-acne-while-using-retin-a.360684/"},{"title":"low dose retin a long term","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/low-dose-retin-a-long-term.349845/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20210521030237/https://looksmax.org/threads/low-dose-retin-a-long-term.349845/"},{"title":"my collagen is so bad any advice other than retin a and vitamin c","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/my-collagen-is-so-bad-any-advice-other-than-retin-a-and-vitamin-c.259305/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"ht